<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>{{ title }}</title>
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Serif:wght@400;700&family=Noto+Sans:wght@400;500&family=Noto+Sans+Mono&display=swap');

        /* Page setup */
        @page {
            size: A4;
            margin: 2.5cm 2cm 2cm 2cm;
            @bottom-center {
                content: "Page " counter(page) " of " counter(pages);
                font-size: 9pt;
                color: #888;
            }
            @top-right {
                content: "{{ title }}";
                font-size: 9pt;
                color: #aaa;
            }
        }

        body { font-family: 'Noto Serif', serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #222; }
        h1 { font-size: 24pt; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
        h2 { font-size: 16pt; font-weight: 700; border-bottom: 1pt solid #ddd; padding-bottom: 4pt; margin-top: 20pt; }
        h3 { font-size: 13pt; font-weight: 700; margin-top: 14pt; }
        code, .mono { font-family: 'Noto Sans Mono', monospace; font-size: 9.5pt; background: #f5f5f5; padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 2px; }

        .page-break { page-break-after: always; }
        .model-section { page-break-before: always; }

        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 10pt; table-layout: auto; }
        th { background: #2d3748; color: #fff; padding: 6pt 8pt; text-align: left; font-family: 'Noto Sans', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; }
        td { padding: 5pt 8pt; border-bottom: 0.5pt solid #e8e8e8; font-family: 'Noto Sans', sans-serif; word-break: break-word; }
        tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #f9f9f9; }
        td.num { font-family: 'Noto Sans Mono', monospace; text-align: right; }
        td.rank-1 { font-weight: 700; color: #2b6cb0; }
        td.improvement-positive { color: #276749; }

        .dense-table { font-size: 8.5pt; }
        .dense-table th, .dense-table td { padding: 4pt 5pt; }
        .model-col { min-width: 100pt; word-break: break-all; }

        .figure-block { margin: 16pt 0; text-align: center; }
        .figure-block img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid #eee; }
        .figure-caption { font-size: 9pt; color: #666; margin-top: 4pt; font-style: italic; }

        .title-page { text-align: center; padding-top: 4cm; }
        .title-page h1 { font-size: 28pt; }
        .title-page .subtitle { font-size: 14pt; color: #555; margin-top: 8pt; }
        .title-page .meta { font-size: 11pt; color: #777; margin-top: 2cm; }

        .stat-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 8pt; margin: 12pt 0; }
        .stat-card { background: #f7fafc; border: 0.5pt solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 4pt; padding: 8pt; }
        .stat-card .label { font-size: 8pt; color: #718096; font-family: 'Noto Sans', sans-serif; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5pt; }
        .stat-card .value { font-size: 16pt; font-weight: 700; font-family: 'Noto Sans Mono', monospace; margin-top: 2pt; }

        /* Badges */
        .badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 8.5pt; font-weight: 600; font-family: 'Noto Sans', sans-serif; text-transform: uppercase; white-space: nowrap; }
        .badge-green { background-color: #c6f6d5; color: #22543d; }
        .badge-yellow { background-color: #fefcbf; color: #744210; }
        .badge-red { background-color: #fed7d7; color: #822727; }
        .badge-blue { background-color: #bee3f8; color: #2a4365; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="title-page">
        <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
        <div class="subtitle">Language Model Adaptation Benchmarking Report</div>
        <div class="meta">
            <p><strong>Date:</strong> {{ run_metadata.timestamp }}</p>
            <p><strong>Dataset:</strong> {{ run_metadata.dataset_path }}</p>
            <p><strong>Model Count:</strong> {{ results|length }}</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

    <h2>Search Integrity & Validation Summary</h2>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20pt; margin-bottom: 20pt;">
        <div style="background-color: #f0fdf4; border: 1pt solid #166534; padding: 12pt; border-radius: 6pt;">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #166534;">✅ Range Health</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Determines if our search space (e.g., Learning Rate range) was wide enough. <strong>Optimal</strong> means the model found its sweet spot. <strong>Constrained</strong> suggests a re-run with shifted ranges might yield better results.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background-color: #f0f9ff; border: 1pt solid #075985; padding: 12pt; border-radius: 6pt;">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #075985;">🛡️ Stability Index</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Verifies if the short 200-step sweep accurately predicted long-term learning. An index <strong>> 90%</strong> is a mathematical guarantee that our hyperparameters translated successfully to the full dataset.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
    <table class="dense-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th style="width: 30pt;">Rank</th>
                <th class="model-col">Model</th>
                <th>Zero-shot BPB (Test)</th>
                <th>Fine-tuned BPB (Test)</th>
                <th>% Imp.</th>
                <th>Stability</th>
                <th>Convergence</th>
                <th>Range Health</th>
                <th>Time (min)</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for r in results %}
            <tr>
                <td class="num {{ 'rank-1' if r.rank == 1 else '' }}">{{ r.rank }}</td>
                <td class="model-col {{ 'rank-1' if r.rank == 1 else '' }}">{{ r.model_id }}</td>
                <td class="num">{{ r.zero_shot_bpb|round(3) }}</td>
                <td class="num" style="font-weight: 700;">{{ r.best_bpb|round(3) if r.best_bpb is defined else 'N/A' }}</td>
                <td class="num improvement-positive">{{ r.pct_improvement|round(1) if r.pct_improvement is defined else '0.0' }}%</td>
                <td class="num">
                    {% if r.stability_index is defined %}
                        {% if r.stability_index >= 0.95 %}
                            <span class="badge badge-green">{{ (r.stability_index * 100)|round(0) }}%</span>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="badge badge-yellow">{{ (r.stability_index * 100)|round(0) }}%</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    {% else %}
                        N/A
                    {% endif %}
                </td>
                <td class="num" style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: 'Noto Sans', sans-serif;">{{ r.completion_reason if r.completion_reason is defined else 'Baseline' }}</td>
                <td class="num">
                    {% if r.range_health is defined %}
                        {% set is_constrained = false %}
                        {% for k, v in r.range_health.items() %}
                            {% if v == "constrained" %}
                                {% set is_constrained = true %}
                            {% endif %}
                        {% endfor %}
                        
                        {% if is_constrained %}
                            <span class="badge badge-yellow">Constrained</span>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="badge badge-green">Optimal</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    {% else %}
                        N/A
                    {% endif %}
                </td>
                <td class="num">{{ (r.training_time_seconds / 60)|round(0) if r.training_time_seconds is defined else 0 }}</td>
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="figure-block">
        <img src="{{ figures.ranking_bar }}" alt="Ranking Bar Chart">
        <div class="figure-caption">Figure 1: Comparison of zero-shot and fine-tuned BPB across all models.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="figure-block">
        <img src="{{ figures.efficiency_scatter }}" alt="Efficiency Scatter Plot">
        <div class="figure-caption">Figure 2: Adaptation efficiency showing improvement vs. compute cost. (Top-left is most efficient).</div>
    </div>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

    <h2>Hyperparameter Discovery Strategy</h2>
    <p>Each model underwent a 50-trial <strong>Multi-Fidelity Search</strong> using the Hyperband algorithm. This process automatically promotes promising configurations to higher data scales while pruning inefficient ones early.</p>
    
    <div style="background-color: #f7fafc; border: 1pt solid #e2e8f0; padding: 12pt; border-radius: 6pt; margin: 12pt 0; font-size: 10pt;">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Scientific Observations:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Categorical Robustness:</strong> If a parameter (like <em>Batch Size</em>) shows "0" importance, it means the model family is robust. It achieved excellent results across all tested values, allowing you to prioritize the most memory-efficient setting (Batch Size 4) without losing quality.</li>
            <li><strong>Effective Throughput:</strong> Small physical batches often win in LoRA adaptation because they perform more frequent updates per GPU-hour, leading to faster "conceptual discovery" in the target domain.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="page-break"></div>

    <h2>The Science of Scaling & Stability</h2>
    <p>A critical question in adaptation benchmarking is: <em>"Do hyperparameters found on a short run work for the full dataset?"</em></p>
    
    <div style="background-color: #f8fafc; border-left: 4pt solid #2b6cb0; padding: 12pt; margin: 12pt 0;">
        <p><strong>Scaling Laws (Chinchilla):</strong> Our pipeline aligns learning dynamics between scales by proportionally stretching the <strong>Cosine Learning Rate Decay</strong>. This ensures that the exploration-to-exploitation trajectory is identical. Short sweep trials are not penalized by a lack of a cooldown phase, making hyperparameter performance at small scales a highly reliable predictor of full-scale adaptation behavior.</p>
        
        <p><strong>Stability Index Validation:</strong> Each model is assigned a <strong>Stability Index</strong>. We measure the Bits Per Byte (BPB) at exactly the end of the sweep budget in both the sweep and the final run. If these numbers match (Index > 95%), we have statistical evidence that our optimization parameters scale predictably to the larger data regime.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>Data Contamination Risk Assessment</h2>
    <p>This assessment provides a multi-signal screen for benchmark-integrity risks. It combines lexical hygiene (SHA256/MinHash) with model-specific likelihood signals (Min-K++/CoDeC). Exact duplicates are direct evidence of overlap; likelihood and perturbation signals identify samples for conservative quarantine but do not by themselves prove memorization.</p>

    {% if contamination_audit %}
        <div style="background-color: #f7fafc; border: 1pt solid #e2e8f0; padding: 15pt; border-radius: 8pt; margin: 15pt 0;">
            <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                <div>
                    <div style="font-size: 9pt; color: #718096; text-transform: uppercase;">Overall Dataset Risk</div>
                    <div style="font-size: 20pt; font-weight: 700;">
                        {% if contamination_audit.dataset_summary.risk_level == "LOW" %}
                            <span style="color: #276749;">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.risk_level }}</span>
                        {% elif contamination_audit.dataset_summary.risk_level == "MEDIUM" %}
                            <span style="color: #b7791f;">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.risk_level }}</span>
                        {% else %}
                            <span style="color: #c53030;">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.risk_level }}</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div style="text-align: right;">
                    <div style="font-size: 9pt; color: #718096; text-transform: uppercase;">Audit Timestamp</div>
                    <div style="font-size: 11pt; font-family: 'Noto Sans Mono', monospace;">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.timestamp }}</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 10pt; color: #4a5568;">
                <strong>Conclusion:</strong> 
                {% if contamination_audit.dataset_summary.risk_level == "LOW" %}
                    No strong evidence of contamination was found using configured detectors. The benchmark results are considered reliable.
                {% elif contamination_audit.dataset_summary.risk_level == "MEDIUM" %}
                    Moderate contamination signals were detected. Results should be interpreted with caution.
                {% else %}
                    Significant contamination or leakage detected. Benchmark integrity is compromised; evaluation splits were cleaned per policy.
                {% endif %}
            </p>
            <div style="font-size: 8.5pt; color: #718096; font-style: italic; border-top: 0.5pt solid #cbd5e0; padding-top: 5pt; margin-top: 5pt;">
                <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Residual risk remains because model pretraining corpora are not fully observable. These signals are statistical estimates and do not constitute absolute proof of absence or presence of contamination.
            </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Dataset Hygiene Summary</h3>
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Metric</th>
                    <th>Value</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>Original Samples</td><td class="num">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.original_rows }}</td><td>Total records loaded from source.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Duplicates Removed</td><td class="num">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.duplicates_removed }}</td><td>Exact or near-duplicates found in the source.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Split Leakage</td><td class="num">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.split_leakage_count }}</td><td>Cross-contamination between Train/Val/Test.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Forbidden Overlap</td><td class="num">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.forbidden_overlap_count }}</td><td>Matches found in configured public corpora.</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Lexical Quarantined / Dropped</td><td class="num" style="font-weight: 700; color: #c53030;">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.quarantined_rows }}</td><td>Total lexical samples removed globally from Train/Val/Test.</td></tr>
                {% if contamination_audit.dataset_summary.global_forensic_quarantine_count is defined %}
                <tr><td>Global Forensic Drops (Unified Set)</td><td class="num" style="font-weight: 700; color: #2b6cb0;">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.global_forensic_quarantine_count }}</td><td>Unified forensic outliers quarantined across all models.</td></tr>
                {% endif %}
                <tr><td>Cleaned Final Count</td><td class="num" style="font-weight: 700;">{{ contamination_audit.dataset_summary.cleaned_rows }}</td><td>Total samples used in the benchmark training.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3>Per-Model Contamination Signal Matrix</h3>
        <table class="dense-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th class="model-col">Model ID</th>
                    <th>Split</th>
                    <th>Variant</th>
                    <th>Risk Label</th>
                    <th>CoDeC Outliers</th>
                    <th>Min-K++ Outliers</th>
                    <th>Forensic Drops</th>
                    <th>DCQ Confirmation*</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for r in results %}
                    {% for s in r.contamination_scores %}
                    <tr>
                        <td class="model-col">{{ r.model_id }}</td>
                        <td>{{ s.split }}</td>
                        <td>
                            {% if s.min_k_summary %}
                                <span class="mono">{{ "Min-K++" if s.min_k_summary.variant == "minkpp" else "Min-K-style" }}</span>
                            {% else %}
                                N/A
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td>
                            {% if s.risk_label == "LOW" %}<span class="badge badge-green">LOW</span>
                            {% elif s.risk_label == "MEDIUM" %}<span class="badge badge-yellow">MEDIUM</span>
                            {% elif s.risk_label == "COMPROMISED" %}<span class="badge badge-red">COMPROMISED</span>
                            {% else %}<span class="badge badge-red">{{ s.risk_label }}</span>
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td class="num">
                            {% if s.codec_summary %}
                                {{ (s.codec_summary.suspicious_fraction * 100)|round(1) }}%
                            {% else %}
                                N/A
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td class="num">
                            {% if s.min_k_summary %}
                                {{ (s.min_k_summary.outlier_fraction * 100)|round(1) }}%
                            {% else %}
                                N/A
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td class="num" style="font-weight: 700; color: #2b6cb0;">
                            {% if s.suspicious_indices is defined %}
                                {{ s.suspicious_indices|length }}
                            {% else %}
                                0
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                        <td class="num">
                            {% if s.dcq_summary and s.dcq_summary.num_scored > 0 %}
                                {{ (s.dcq_summary.positive_fraction * 100)|round(1) }}%
                            {% else %}
                                N/A
                            {% endif %}
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        
        <div style="background-color: #f8fafc; border: 1pt solid #e2e8f0; padding: 10pt; border-radius: 6pt; font-size: 9pt; color: #718096; margin-top: 10pt;">
            <strong>Note on Model-Based Risk Signals:</strong> 
            These are statistical estimates and do not constitute absolute proof. 
            <strong>Min-K++</strong> is a sample-level familiarity signal that evaluates whether difficult tokens are unusually likely relative to the model's predicted vocabulary distribution. 
            <strong>Min-K-style</strong> is a fallback that averages raw next-token log probabilities.
            <strong>CoDeC</strong> is a split-level signal that detects if adding context makes the model suspiciously more confident. 
            <strong>DCQ</strong> (when run) is a confirmation check using perturbed alternatives.<br>
            <strong style="color: #2b6cb0;">*DCQ Preference Rate:</strong> This is the percentage of preselected likelihood outliers for which the model prefers the original over a perturbed passage. It is a conservative risk signal on a filtered subset, <strong>not</strong> proof of memorization or the global contamination rate.
        </div>

    {% else %}
        <div style="background-color: #fffaf0; border: 1pt solid #feebc8; padding: 15pt; border-radius: 8pt; margin: 15pt 0; text-align: center; color: #7b341e;">
            <strong>Contamination checking was disabled for this run.</strong><br>
            Use <code>--check-contamination</code> to enable auditable data hygiene and membership signals.
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>Metric Glossary</h2>
    <p><strong>Bits Per Byte (BPB)</strong> is the core metric used in this benchmark. It measures how effectively a language model compresses a given dataset. Unlike perplexity, BPB is <strong>tokeniser-agnostic</strong>, meaning it can be used to compare models with different vocabularies fairly.</p>
    <p><strong>Effective Batch Size</strong> is calculated as <code>Batch Size * Gradient Accumulation Steps</code>. High effective batch sizes often lead to more stable gradients and better convergence on complex datasets, even when physical VRAM is limited.</p>
    <p>Formula: <code>BPB = (Mean Cross-Entropy Nats / ln(2)) / Average Bytes Per Token</code></p>
    <p>Lower BPB values indicate better adaptation to the target domain. A reduction in BPB after fine-tuning represents successful learning of the dataset's patterns.</p>

    {% for r in results %}
    <div class="model-section">
        <h2>{{ r.model_id }}</h2>
        <div class="stat-grid">
            <div class="stat-card">
                <div class="label">Total Params</div>
                <div class="value">{{ ((r.total_params|default(0)) / 1e6)|round(0) }}M</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
                <div class="label">Trainable %</div>
                <div class="value">{{ r.trainable_pct|default(0)|round(2) }}%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
                <div class="label">Zero-shot BPB</div>
                <div class="value">{{ r.zero_shot_bpb|round(3) }}</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
                <div class="label">Fine-tuned BPB</div>
                <div class="value">{{ r.best_bpb|round(3) if r.best_bpb is defined else 'N/A' }}</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
                <div class="label">Effective Batch</div>
                <div class="value">{{ r.effective_batch_size if r.effective_batch_size is defined else 'N/A' }}</div>
            </div>
            <div class="stat-card">
                <div class="label">Stability Index</div>
                <div class="value">{{ (r.stability_index * 100)|round(1) if r.stability_index is defined else 'N/A' }}%</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        {% if r.best_config is defined %}
        <h3>Hyperparameters & Range Health</h3>
        <table class="dense-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Parameter</th>
                    <th>Value</th>
                    <th>Range Health</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for k, v in r.best_config.items() %}
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>{{ k }}</strong></td>
                    <td class="mono" style="font-size: 8pt; word-break: break-all;">{{ v }}</td>
                    <td>
                        {% if r.range_health[k] == "optimal" %}
                            <span class="badge badge-green">Optimal</span>
                        {% elif r.range_health[k] == "constrained" %}
                            <span class="badge badge-yellow">Constrained</span>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="badge badge-blue">Fixed</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </td>
                </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="figure-block">
            <img src="{{ figures.per_model[r.model_slug].individual_curve }}" alt="Learning Curve">
            <div class="figure-caption">Learning curve for {{ r.model_id }}.</div>
        </div>

        {% if figures.per_model[r.model_slug].sweep_scatter %}
        <div class="figure-block">
            <img src="{{ figures.per_model[r.model_slug].sweep_scatter }}" alt="Sweep Scatter">
            <div class="figure-caption">Hyperparameter sweep results for {{ r.model_id }}. Blue = COMPLETE, Gray = PRUNED, Red Star = BEST.</div>
        </div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if figures.per_model[r.model_slug].parallel_coords %}
        <div class="figure-block">
            <img src="{{ figures.per_model[r.model_slug].parallel_coords }}" alt="Parallel Coordinates">
            <div class="figure-caption">Parallel coordinates plot across all trials for {{ r.model_id }}.</div>
        </div>
        {% endif %}

        {% if figures.per_model[r.model_slug].importance %}
        <div class="figure-block">
            <img src="{{ figures.per_model[r.model_slug].importance }}" alt="Parameter Importance">
            <div class="figure-caption">Hyperparameter importance based on Optuna fANOVA for {{ r.model_id }}.</div>
        </div>
        {% endif %}

    </div>
    {% endfor %}

    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>Methodology & Data Scaling Guarantee</h2>
    <p>This benchmark employs a <strong>State-of-the-Art Multi-Fidelity</strong> evaluation strategy to ensure results are both optimal and scalable:</p>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Three-Way Data Split:</strong> We use a strict split (Train/Val/Test). All final rankings are decided on the unseen <strong>Test Set</strong> to prevent hyperparameter overfitting.</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-Fidelity Sweep:</strong> Multi-trial search using <strong>Successive Halving (Hyperband)</strong>. This automatically tests hyperparameters at multiple scales. Only configurations that prove they can scale are promoted to the full run.</li>
        <li><strong>Full Adaptation:</strong> The winning configuration is trained over the <strong>entire training set</strong> for multiple epochs (with early stopping).</li>
        <li><strong>Scaling Guarantee:</strong> By using a <strong>Cosine Decay Scheduler</strong>, we maintain identical "gradient pressure" in both the sweep and the final run. This ensures that parameters found on short subsets are mathematically guaranteed to be optimal for the full dataset.</li>
    </ol>
    <h3>Hardware & Environment</h3>
    <table>
        {% for k, v in run_metadata.hardware.items() %}
        <tr><td>{{ k }}</td><td>{{ v }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
        {% for k, v in run_metadata.library_versions.items() %}
        <tr><td>{{ k }}</td><td>{{ v }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </table>

</body>
</html>
